---
title: How to set default Quotation Template
sidebar:
  order: 11
---
**To set a default template for your quotations, follow these steps:**

1. **Access the Settings Menu**

   - **Click on your profile avatar or name at the top right of the dashboard.**
   - **From the dropdown menu, select Settings.**

1. **Navigate to Quotation Settings**

   - **In the left sidebar, click on Quotations Settings.**

1. **Select the Template Tab**

   - **Once on the Quotation Settings page, click on the Template tab at the top.**

1. **Choose a Template**

   - **Under Change Template, you will see a selection of different templates with previews.**
   - **Browse through the template options and review the design, layout, and format of each.**

1. **Set the Default Template**

   - **Click on your preferred template to select it as the default.**
   - **Once selected, the template will automatically apply to all new quotations created in the system.**

1. **Save Changes**

   - **If there is a save option, ensure you click Save Changes to confirm your selection.**

**The chosen default template will now be used for all your quotations, providing a consistent and professional layout for your business documents.**
